{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, while image-only resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208. This establishes RNA as the dominant modality and multiprofile+avgpool as the best RNA pipeline, but leaves the critical question of whether multimodal fusion can improve upon the RNA-only baseline. Question being tested: Does adding image features (resnet50) via simple concat fusion to the best RNA configuration (multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) yield any gain over 0.591, or does the weak image signal (0.208 standalone) degrade performance? Why this is the best next experiment: config_018 is the minimal, most direct extension of our top configuration—identical RNA encoder, profile, and aggregation—so any performance delta is cleanly attributable to the image modality and fusion. It resolves the highest-priority uncertainty (does multimodal help at all?) before spending budget on more complex variants (weighted fusion, ViT-L, alternative RNA encoders). If it helps, we exploit further; if it hurts, we can refocus on RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) with confidence that image is not the bottleneck."
}

